{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block content %}
<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto p-4 md:p-6 w-full font-mono">

  <!-- Header Card / Window Frame -->
  <div class="retro-card p-0 mb-6">
    <div class="window-header flex items-center justify-between p-2">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <span>🔒</span>
        <span class="font-bold">[:&gt; PRIVACY_POLICY.TXT - Cyberspace Data Protection &amp; SMS Policy]</span>
      </div>
      <a href="/" class="pixel-btn pixel-btn--sm text-xs py-0.5 px-2 text-white">
        [ &lt; Return to Station ]
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="p-4 md:p-6 text-xs md:text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-6">

      <!-- Effective Date Bar -->
      <div class="bg-black border border-main p-3 text-prompt flex items-center justify-between flex-wrap gap-2 text-xs">
        <div><strong>DOCUMENT ID:</strong> NEOGRAM-PRIVACY-2026.1</div>
        <div><strong>EFFECTIVE DATE:</strong> October 22, 2026</div>
        <div><strong>SERVICE URL:</strong> https://neogram.club</div>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 1: Overview & Philosophy -->
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-prompt text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border-b border-main pb-1">
          1. Privacy Philosophy &amp; Overview
        </h2>
        <p>
          At <strong>Neogram</strong> ("we", "us", or "our"), hosted at <a href="https://neogram.club" class="text-mac underline">https://neogram.club</a>, we believe in radical digital privacy, minimal data retention, and authentic 90s-era decentralization. We collect only the minimum telemetry strictly necessary to authenticate your station, deliver one-time verification codes, and compile your photo galleries directly to your personal static site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: STRICT Mobile & SMS Privacy Policy (Carrier Mandate) -->
      <section class="space-y-3 bg-black border-2 border-prompt p-4">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-prompt font-bold text-sm">
          <span>📱</span>
          <h3>2. Mobile Information &amp; SMS Privacy Policy (Strict Zero-Sharing Guarantee)</h3>
        </div>

        <p class="text-white font-bold">
          We deeply respect your mobile privacy. The following terms govern all mobile phone numbers and SMS consent data collected by Neogram:
        </p>

        <div class="bg-[#001100] border border-prompt p-3 text-prompt space-y-2 text-xs">
          <p class="font-bold uppercase tracking-wide">
            <strong>STRICT NON-DISCLOSURE CLAUSE:</strong>
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>No mobile information will be shared with third parties/affiliates for marketing/promotional purposes. All the above categories exclude text messaging originator opt-in data and consent; this information will not be shared with any third parties.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-2 pl-2">
          <p>
            <strong>2.1 Purpose of Mobile Phone Collection:</strong> Mobile telephone numbers provided during login or registration are utilized solely and exclusively for two-factor authentication, identity verification, and transmitting single-use one-time password (OTP) authorization keys requested by you.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>2.2 No Marketing or Reselling:</strong> We do not sell, rent, lease, license, or disclose phone numbers or text messaging opt-in consent to any marketing agencies, data brokers, advertising networks, or third-party affiliates under any circumstances.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>2.3 Infrastructure Subprocessors:</strong> Phone numbers are transmitted securely via TLS encryption to our trusted telecommunications transit provider (Twilio Inc.) solely to execute carrier delivery of the one-time authentication text message you requested.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: Information We Collect -->
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-prompt text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border-b border-main pb-1">
          3. Information We Collect
        </h2>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 pl-2 text-muted">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">Account Authentication Credentials:</strong> Your email address or mobile phone number, utilized exclusively to dispatch one-time login OTP codes. We do not store permanent account passwords.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">Public Cyberspace Identity:</strong> Your public call-sign handle (<code>@handle</code>), avatar, status message, and immutable numeric node identifier (<code>#UIN</code>) used across Neogram social widgets and chat.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">Encrypted Deployment Keys:</strong> If you connect remote static publishing targets (e.g. Neocities API keys, GitHub tokens, or SFTP passwords), these credentials are stored encrypted at rest using AES-256-GCM.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4: Zero Server Media Storage -->
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-prompt text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border-b border-main pb-1">
          4. Zero Server Media Retention (0 MB)
        </h2>
        <p>
          Unlike centralized social networks, Neogram maintains a strict <strong>Zero Local Media Retention</strong> invariant:
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted">
          When you snap or upload a photo, image processing (resizing, WebP compression, and retro CRT scanline shader generation) is performed ephemerally in server memory and isolated build staging. The instant the generated files are uploaded to your personal static hosting provider (e.g. Neocities), <strong>the local media files are permanently deleted from our server disk</strong>. Our local server disk retention returns to 0 bytes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5: Ephemeral Chat Architecture (NIM) -->
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-prompt text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border-b border-main pb-1">
          5. Neogram Instant Messenger (NIM) Ephemeral Architecture
        </h2>
        <p>
          Real-time chat messages routed via WebSockets are processed strictly in server memory without permanent database retention. If a recipient is offline, the message is temporarily held in an encrypted ephemeral queue for up to 24 hours. The instant the recipient establishes a connection, the message is delivered and <strong>immediately hard-deleted from the database</strong>. 100% of persistent chat history resides strictly in client-side browser storage (<code>localStorage</code>), which you can clear at any time.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 6: Cookies & Tracking -->
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-prompt text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border-b border-main pb-1">
          6. Cookies &amp; Tracking Technologies
        </h2>
        <p>
          Neogram uses strictly essential, first-party HTTP-only session cookies (<code>neogram_session</code>) to maintain your login status. We employ zero third-party advertising cookies, zero analytics trackers, and zero cross-site behavioral tracking scripts.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 7: Data Retention & Deletion Rights -->
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-prompt text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border-b border-main pb-1">
          7. Data Retention &amp; User Deletion Rights
        </h2>
        <p>
          You have the right to request the inspection, correction, or complete deletion of your account record and associated metadata from our database. To request account deletion or data removal, contact us at <a href="mailto:auth@neogram.club" class="text-prompt underline">auth@neogram.club</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 8: Contact -->
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-prompt text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border-b border-main pb-1">
          8. Contact &amp; Privacy Officer
        </h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions, concerns, or requests regarding this Privacy Policy or your personal data, please contact:
        </p>
        <div class="bg-black border border-main p-3 text-xs space-y-1">
          <div><strong>PRIVACY OFFICER:</strong> Neogram Network Security</div>
          <div><strong>EMAIL:</strong> <a href="mailto:auth@neogram.club" class="text-prompt underline">auth@neogram.club</a></div>
          <div><strong>WEBSITE:</strong> <a href="https://neogram.club" class="text-mac underline">https://neogram.club</a></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Footer Quick Links -->
      <div class="pt-4 border-t border-main flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-muted flex-wrap gap-2">
        <div>&copy; 2026 Neogram. All rights reserved.</div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <a href="/terms" class="text-mac underline hover:text-white">Terms of Service &gt;&gt;</a>
          <a href="/login" class="text-prompt underline hover:text-white">Terminal Login &gt;&gt;</a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

</div>
{% endblock %}
